   "source": [
    "### Artificially increase the signal in the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "The signal for detecting admission in the college data is fairly weak — too weak for demonstration purposes. Below, we not only multiply the dataset by 10, but also add an artificial signal for detecting `admit` to the `gpa` column. \n",
    "\n",
    "*Obviously* you would never do this to your real data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "admit = admissions[admissions.prestige == 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "admit = pd.concat([admit]*10, axis=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "admit.loc[admit.admit == 1, 'gpa'] += np.random.random(size=admit[admit.admit == 1].shape[0])\n",
    "admit.loc[admit.admit == 0, 'gpa'] -= np.random.random(size=admit[admit.admit == 0].shape[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "*The addition of random signal will cause slight variance in our results throughout the lesson.*"
   ]
  },
