   "source": [
    "<a id='solving-beta'></a>\n",
    "## Solving For the Beta Coefficients\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "Logistic regression minimizes the \"deviance,\" which is similar to the residual sum of squares in linear regression. There's not a closed-form solution to the beta coefficients like in linear regression and the betas are found through optimization procedures.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you're particularly interested in the math, here are two helpful resources:\n",
    "\n",
    "[A good blog post on the logistic regression beta coefficient derivation](http://www.win-vector.com/blog/2011/09/the-simpler-derivation-of-logistic-regression/).\n",
    "\n",
    "[This paper is also a good reference](https://www.stat.cmu.edu/~cshalizi/402/lectures/14-logistic-regression/lecture-14.pdf).\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
